{"id": "EUVD-2026-104692", "enisaUuid": "2ff5fe95-fb07-34be-8c49-ee30adb937b9", "description": "Letta through 0.16.8 ships a compose.yaml that does not enable LETTA_SERVER_SECURE, so the password middleware is never added and all API routes are unauthenticated, and it exposes a superuser PostgreSQL port with default credentials. Remote attackers can execute arbitrary Python via POST /v1/tools/run, manage /v1/admin users, or run OS commands via COPY PROGRAM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:07:28", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.lasso.security/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-77936", "https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/blob/1131535716e8a31c9a437f8695e25ac98f203a24/compose.yaml#L17", "https://github.com/letta-ai/letta/blob/1131535716e8a31c9a437f8695e25ac98f203a24/letta/server/rest_api/app.py#L799", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/letta-through-0.16.8-insecure-default-configuration-unauthenticated-api-and-postgresql-access"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g524-hhf9-5x95", "CVE-2026-77936"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8d57b36a-fd42-33e7-9b4e-e5ef30825370", "product": {"name": "letta", "vendor": {"name": "letta-ai"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.16.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b5a7ba42-8763-3495-bf65-ff331fb03934", "vendor": {"name": "letta-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}